      "mergeID": "6537de5719d38e1982ff1c26",
      "mergedPostDetails": "0. Find a specific Avatar for which this happens\n\n1. Open VRChat\n\n2. Load into a World\n\n3. Go into the Menu for Avatar Scaling\n\n4. Enter the Radial\n\n5. The avatar changes size as you enter your new size as usual\n\n6. Confirm the Change\n\n7. Your Avatar Size is reset to your regular Avatar size.\n\nSome testing steps I took so far: \n\n- I removed all Animators from my avatar, but the issue seems to persist regardless\n\n- I looked if all my uploaded avatars are affected, but that doesn't seem to be the case as I found an unaffected one.\n\n- I removed all SkinnedMeshRenderers, and the issue still persists.\n\n- I removed a lot of custom armature, and the issue still persists.\n\n- Removing the Animator->Avatar Reference makes scaling work again\n\nI uploaded a test avatar that has this issue with the id: avtr_cac667a4-34d8-48e4-baf7-2d75269f86f4  (use Prismic's Avatar World to get it, by directly entering the id)\n\nI also tested the avatar on a second computer and it this behavior also happens there.\n\nTested on builds 1348, 1350 and 1370",
      "mergedPostTitle": "[1370/1350/1348] Avatar Scaling breaks on certain avatars",
